Sprite catalog provenance
=========================

`catalog.json` in this directory (schema `meetropolis-sprite-catalog/v6`)
is produced through the asset-atelier catalog path in `tools/asset-lab/`
(`scripts/sprite-catalog.ts`, which reads the existing catalog as its base
and applies `buildAtelierCatalog` from `src/avatar-catalog.ts` with the
Atelier raster additions). The underlying pixel lineage comes from the
Meetropolis sprite generator at `tools/sprite-generator/` (engine.py,
poses.py, generate.py, export_catalog.py and the `catalogs/` package),
whose sources carry `SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only` and stay
AGPL-3.0-only. The six character PNGs remain the Python generator's
output (`generate.py`).

This generated `catalog.json` is licensed under the MIT License, consistent
with the surrounding `@meetropolis/shared` package (see ../package.json and
../LICENSE). Tiamat UG holds the copyright in both the generator and this
generated output and, as the copyright holder, licenses this file under MIT.
The AGPL-3.0 copyleft binds third parties who run the generator on their own;
it does not constrain the copyright holder's licensing of its own output.

It is vendored here so the shared composer, the AGPL-3.0 server and the web
editor all read one identical contract (guaranteeing preview == the
server-composited sheet).

Do not hand-edit `catalog.json`. Regenerate the current v6 catalog
through the asset-atelier path from the repository root (the legacy
Python v5 export below is no longer authoritative for this file):

    npm --prefix tools/asset-lab run catalog:build    # -> packages/shared/sprite/catalog.json (v6)
    npm --prefix tools/asset-lab run catalog:check    # verify it is up to date

The legacy Python v5 export (`python3 export_catalog.py` in
`tools/sprite-generator/`) remains documented in
`tools/sprite-generator/README.md` and is no longer the authoritative
generation for the current v6 catalog.

The pixel basis is authored procedurally from the grid templates in
`tools/sprite-generator/catalogs/`; no third-party pixel data is read,
sampled, or referenced. The current v6 catalog additionally contains the
Atelier raster additions from the atelier path above.
